# t01_1_inventory.sparql — owl:sameAs residue, by graph. READ-ONLY.
#
# Run BEFORE t01_2_sweep and read the result before writing anything:
#
#   - A file-backed authority graph in the list means the rs-ldp deploy or the
#     restart did not land — fix the FILES (deploy.sh + restart), do not sweep
#     that graph here. Force-load would silently revert a DB-side rewrite on
#     the next boot (forceLDPLoadFromStorages=runtime).
#   - Only graphs you OWN go into 02's VALUES allowlist. Ontology graphs and
#     offline-loaded external graphs stay out (load-once; a rewrite there is
#     permanent drift in axioms we don't own).
#   - Zero rows => nothing to sweep, go straight to checks.sh verify.
#
# Usage:
#     curl -s -u admin:admin "$SPARQL" --data-urlencode "query=$(cat t01_1_inventory.sparql)"
#
# Dev observed 2026-08-13 (after full deploy+restart): one graph,
# <http://www.researchspace.org/resource/g/data>, 30 triples (murtenpanorama
# place entities -> Wikidata/VIAF/GND/DBpedia; authored by the old owl_sameAs
# form field).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
SELECT ?g (COUNT(*) AS ?n)
WHERE { GRAPH ?g { ?s owl:sameAs ?o } }
GROUP BY ?g
ORDER BY DESC(?n)
